# --- Build artifacts ---
/bin/
/awsbnkctl
*.test
*.out
*.exe
*.exe~

# --- OS / editor ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*.swo
.vscode/
.idea/

# --- Language toolchain caches ---
node_modules/
package-lock.json
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

# --- awsbnkctl-managed cluster state (never commit) ---
# Per-cluster kubeconfig, IDs cache, ephemeral keys.
.awsbnkctl/

# --- BNK supply-chain credentials (never commit) ---
# Operator-supplied per cluster.yaml; grant FAR pull + license rights.
cne_pull_64.json
*.jwt

# --- Release / build outputs ---
dist/

# --- Generated HTML mirrors of Markdown docs (do not track) ---
docs/DEMOS.html

# --- Local environment overrides ---
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# --- Internal dev tooling (not for public repo) ---
# AI-assisted dev framework (MAF, claude-only target); lives on local disk only.
.agent/
.claude/
CLAUDE.local.md

# --- MAF framework operational artifacts (installer-managed) ---
# Only relevant if .agent/ is ever versioned; kept so a future opt-in to
# tracking framework tooling doesn't also pick up runtime/session junk.
.agent/tmp/
.agent/cache/
.agent/**/*.maf.new
.agent/install-state.yaml

# --- Internal debugging / audit notes ---
# Live-cluster captures contain AWS resource IDs + private IPs.
docs/audits/

# --- Internal engineering notes (not for public repo) ---
# Design specs (internal "why we built it" narratives) and feasibility spikes
# (the latter capture live AWS resource IDs + private IPs). Local-only.
docs/design/
docs/spikes/

# --- Demo material (gitignored presentation packet + diagrams) ---
docs/demo/

# --- Compiled tool binaries (build locally; don't commit) ---
/tools/ciwatch/ciwatch
/tools/sprintwatch/sprintwatch

# --- HuggingFace token (gated model auth; never commit) ---
.hf_token

# --- Architecture decision records (local-only) ---
# ADRs capture in-flight design debate, including rejected options and candid
# assessments of gaps. Kept off the public repo like docs/design/ and docs/spikes/;
# the settled outcome belongs in docs/ARCHITECTURE.md instead.
docs/adr/

# --- Internal remediation tracker (local-only) ---
# Maintainer-facing punch list: open defects, unmerged security items, and repo
# housekeeping. Naming an unfixed security issue in a public repo hands a reader
# a map of where we are weak, so this stays local. Anything in it that users need
# belongs in the issue tracker or the docs proper.
docs/REMEDIATION.md
*.maf.new
node_modules/
clusters/
*.orig
patch.diff
.agentcore-network-env.json
.govulncheck-ignore.sh

